[SIZE="4"][B]About[/B][/SIZE]

This is an unofficial TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 build for the [B]LG L50 D213[/B] (codename [B]luv50ss[/B], MediaTek [B]MT6572[/B]). It uses the unmodified stock LG kernel from firmware D21310c and is built from the Android 4.4 OmniROM/TWRP tree, with the native 480x800 theme (no scaling).

[COLOR="Red"][B]Only for the LG L50 D213. Do not flash it on the D210, D221, D227 or any other L50 variant.[/B][/COLOR]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Requires root and the patched LK.[/B][/COLOR] The stock D213 bootloader refuses unsigned recovery images and shows [I]"ERROR: Boot cerification verify <-1>"[/I]. Follow this guide first:
[URL=""][GUIDE] How To Root and Unlock the Bootloader LG L50 D213 (MT6572)[/URL]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status[/B][/SIZE]

Tested on real hardware, D213 on firmware D21310c with the patched LK:

[LIST]
[*]Boot to recovery, display and touchscreen
[*]ADB in recovery
[*]MTP (copy files from the PC while in recovery)
[*]Mount /system, /data and /cache
[*]External microSD (vfat), mounted and readable
[*]Install ZIP packages (used to install the LineageOS 11 ROM for this phone)
[*]Wipe Cache and Dalvik cache
[*]Settings are saved (stored in /data/media/0/TWRP)
[*]Reboot to System returns to Android (no recovery loop)
[/LIST]

[B]Not tested yet:[/B] a full backup-to-restore cycle. Do not rely on a TWRP backup as your only copy until someone confirms a restore.

[B]Not included:[/B] exFAT and decryption of an encrypted /data.

[SIZE="4"][B]Important notes[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Internal storage lives in /data/media.[/B] "Wipe > Factory Reset" and "Wipe Data" keep your internal storage (photos, downloads) by design. "Format Data" erases it.
[*][B]Do not rely on the NVRAM, Uboot and Sec_RO backup entries yet.[/B] They use MTK character devices and have not been verified. Back up your IMEI, NVRAM and calibration partitions with the [I]dd[/I] commands from Step 2 of the root guide instead, and keep them on your PC.
[*][B]Never format /protect_f or /protect_s[/B] (mmcblk0p2 and mmcblk0p3). They hold RF calibration and modem data; without them the phone loses the network.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]

[B]Before starting:[/B] the phone must be rooted and running the patched LK (see the guide above), with USB debugging enabled.

[B]1. Back up the current recovery:[/B]
[CODE]adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/dev/recovery of=/sdcard/recovery-stock.img bs=512 count=20480'"
adb pull /sdcard/recovery-stock.img[/CODE]

[B]2. Flash TWRP:[/B]
[CODE]adb push twrp-3.1.1-0.1-luv50ss.img /sdcard/twrp.img
adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/sdcard/twrp.img of=/dev/recovery bs=512; sync'"[/CODE]

[B]3. Verify the readback before rebooting:[/B]
[CODE]adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/dev/recovery bs=512 count=16096 | md5sum'"[/CODE]
It must print [B]9a01f28ce1cb7a7e56f9c07653da85ec[/B]. [COLOR="Red"][B]If it does not match, do NOT reboot:[/B][/COLOR] repeat Step 2.

[I]/dev/recovery[/I] is an MTK character device: always read it with [I]bs=512[/I] and an explicit [I]count[/I].

[SIZE="4"][B]Entering recovery[/B][/SIZE]

From Android or from TWRP:
[CODE]adb reboot recovery[/CODE]

On LineageOS 11 you can also enable [I]Settings > Developer options > Advanced reboot[/I] and choose Recovery from the power menu. The hardware key path on this phone goes through LG's factory reset screen, so it is not recommended.

